Dear AACRAID SCSI RAID DRIVER maintainers,

I might find a bug concerning the scsi raid controller in the
**2.6.25.3** kernel.

The bug description is like this:
When I started the boot process with "AACRAID SCSI RAID DRIVER",
the kernel got into panic reporting the following message.
********************************************
... # the whole message is in the attached log file: 2.6.25.3_bug_scsi.txt
scsi2 : aacraid
scsi 2:0:0:0: Direct-Access Adaptec 2120S Mirror V1.0 PQ: 0 ANSI: 2
aac_srb: aac_fib_send failed with status: 8195
aac_srb: aac_fib_send failed with status: 8195
... # infinite loop
********************************************
I could not find the reason of this panic.

Respectfully,

